'''''Senecio nemorensis''''' is a species of [[perennial plant]] from the family [[Asteraceae]] that can reach {{convert|2|m}} in height. The plant is native to [[Europe]] and [[Asia]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.inaturalist.org/listed_taxa/10874854 |title= Alpine Ragwort (Senecio nemorensis) (Europe Check List)|publisher=iNaturalist|access-date=28 October 2017}}</ref> where it can be found growing at elevation {{convert|800|-|1800|m}}.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pfaf.org/User/Plant.aspx?LatinName=Senecio+nemorensis |title=Senecio nemorensis|publisher=Plants For A Future|access-date=28 October 2017}}</ref>

